Revision history for GobanFTP

1.000  2026-05-19
  - Entered the v1.0 / package 1.000 final-candidate identity after the
    refreshed `1.000_001` development-freeze matrix passed; this is not a tag,
    publication event, P14 completion claim, or release-ready declaration.
  - Added local `gobanftp play --tui` terminal play as a non-consensus
    input/display surface over the existing play publish path, with keyboard,
    SGR mouse, one-publish lockout, and pty smoke coverage.
  - Added verifier-local signed-HMAC operation support through `gobanftp v1
    keygen`, `gobanftp v1 attest`, and
    `gobanftp v1 witness --trusted-hmac-key-file`, keeping HMAC secrets out of
    stdout, diagnostics, public attestations, filenames, and unsigned replay.
  - Added a read-only signed-HMAC substrate overlay witness path, so
    `signed-hmac-goftp1` can verify the same explicit HMAC attestations after
    local, FTP, Git-tree, DNS-record, or WebDAV read normalization while keeping
    publish authorization and production identity lifecycle out of scope.
  - Added verifier-local `GOFTP-HMAC-PUBLISH/1` publish token generation and
    verification, freezing fixture publish-purpose lifecycle semantics where
    only trusted selectors may authorize new material while rotated, revoked,
    and expired selectors fail closed.
  - Began v1.0/P14 development after skipping the public v0.2 / package 0.002
    release candidate.
  - Recorded a fresh clean-checkout `1.000_001` development-freeze matrix for
    commit 1f5f646921f675c93e25819cb3cf3652f5d6bebe, including the P14 claim
    audit gate, distribution archive evidence, disttest, and distcheck; this
    remains development evidence only, not a final stable v1.0 artifact.
  - Recorded a fresh clean-checkout `1.000_001` development-freeze matrix for
    commit e1c8b4036ce9bf2260455b0aa0834df544393845 after the source-art
    arch-gate, bad-signature public poison vector, and dist hygiene gate landed;
    this remains development evidence only, not a final stable v1.0 artifact.
  - Added `t/p14-claim-audit.t` as a release-text claim-boundary gate for the
    current P14 documents, restore record, and changelog, without declaring
    P14/v1.0 complete or adding Git publish, live DNS, hosted Web UI,
    interactive TUI, or final release capability.
  - Added a core `bad-signature` attack fixture and public non-consensus poison
    vector proving unsigned `GOFTP/1` ignores invalid sidecar signatures while
    preserving the same root, replay, board projection, and SGF truth.
  - Added a dist manifest hygiene gate proving local restore memory, build
    products, `MYMETA.*`, and stale distribution artifacts stay out of the
    source manifest and release archive checks.
  - Added a hidden ASCII arch-gate source-art easter egg to the smoke wrapper,
    with tests asserting the current marker is comment-only, smoke output does
    not emit it, and existing source-art invariance checks keep wrapper art
    outside replay truth.
  - Clarified that `unicode-name`, `path-traversal-name`, and `huge-directory`
    are deferred boundary attack topics, not current v1.0 public vector claims.
  - Promoted `git-tree-goftp1` to read-only runtime admission through
    `GOBANFTP_STORE=git-tree`, enumerating direct Git tree children under
    `<game>/events` while keeping blob bytes, commit metadata, sidecars,
    projections, tmp entries, and Git publish semantics outside consensus.
  - Promoted `dns-record-goftp1` to read-only runtime admission over local or
    otherwise declared record files through `GOBANFTP_STORE=dns-record`, while
    excluding live DNS, AXFR, DNSSEC trust, provider APIs, dynamic updates,
    record publishing, TTLs, ordering, cache state, and provider metadata from
    consensus claims.
  - Added a mock-tested WebDAV store backend that reads `events/` with
    `PROPFIND Depth: 1` and publishes by zero-byte `tmp/` resource plus `MOVE`
    and fresh `PROPFIND` confirmation.
  - Promoted `webdav-goftp1` to an implemented transport-auth profile while
    keeping WebDAV metadata, locks, resource bodies, sidecars, projections, and
    temporary entries outside replay consensus.
  - Documented WebDAV environment configuration and added CLI parity coverage
    for play, watch, SGF, and publish-through-play flows.
  - Added the first v1 profile attack fixture, proving WebDAV metadata,
    body-like PROPFIND row fields, locks, wrong-game hrefs, shadow resources,
    recursive hrefs, duplicates, order, and percent-decoding hazards do not
    change the witness.
  - Added a focused WebDAV href traversal fixture proving raw and percent-encoded
    dot segments cannot smuggle extra events into the profile witness.
  - Added a signed-HMAC payload mismatch fixture proving a trusted MAC over a
    different game descriptor still fails closed at the signed profile gate.
  - Added a signed-HMAC game descriptor mismatch fixture proving a public
    attestation record cannot claim another game descriptor.
  - Added a core `bad-mtime` attack fixture proving event file mtimes do not
    affect replay or `event_set_root`.
  - Added a showcase smoke gate for the public shrine, fork, source-art, and
    unsigned `local-goftp1` v1 witness demonstration path.
  - Added v1 cross-substrate golden vectors for future event versions, missing
    parents, and wrong-player rule failures.
  - Expanded unsigned v1 witness golden vectors to freeze profile, adapter,
    raw, normalized, accepted, rejected, and diagnostic count fields.
  - Hardened unsigned and signed-HMAC witness golden vectors with self-contained
    input names, replay diagnostics, rejected diagnostics, and rendered board,
    verdict, listing, and SGF projection text while keeping HMAC secrets out of
    public vectors.
  - Added v1 replay-invariant golden vectors for illegal sibling isolation,
    invalid root preflight diagnostics, and outsider ACK rejection without
    changing the canonical move line.
  - Expanded v1 replay-invariant golden vectors for capture, suicide rejection,
    bounds parse rejection, single pass, two-pass terminal play, resign
    terminal play, simple-ko superko rejection, ack-assisted fork choice,
    malformed basenames, parent-is-ACK rejection, dangling ACK targets, and ACK
    targets that are themselves ACKs.
  - Added a DNS owner-poison v1 profile attack fixture proving wrong-owner and
    ownerless TXT records cannot smuggle event basenames into the witness.
  - Reworked the README into a release-shaped showcase entrypoint while keeping
    `v0.1`, `v1.0/P14`, signed-HMAC, WebDAV, and deferred-surface boundaries
    explicit.
  - Added a signed-HMAC injected-event fixture proving an unsigned event with a
    valid filename event id is rejected by the signed profile gate while the
    accepted signed chain keeps the same root, replay, board, and SGF.
  - Added a Git-tree path and metadata poison fixture proving commit metadata,
    refs, modes, object ids, object sizes, sidecars, projections, tmp entries,
    recursive paths, wrong-game paths, and duplicates do not change the profile
    witness.
  - Added a WebDAV publish-failure fixture and CLI parity gates proving existing
    final names, delayed MOVE visibility, hard 423 failures, zero-byte temporary
    payloads, retry bounds, and tmp debris do not create hidden witness truth or
    leak bearer tokens.
  - Added fixture-only `gobanftp v1 keyid --fixture` support for `GOFTP-KEY/1`
    public key ids, keeping public key metadata separate from HMAC secrets,
    signatures, trust, and unsigned replay truth.
  - Added fixture-only `gobanftp v1 trust-report --fixture` support for public
    trust TSV summaries, proving trusted, rotated, revoked, and expired key
    rows remain advisory and do not alter unsigned witness truth.
  - Defined the signed-HMAC/trust bridge boundary: `signed-hmac-goftp1` keeps
    explicit HMAC selectors separate from public `GOFTP-KEY/1` `k1.` identities
    and records deterministic trust lifecycle semantics before enforcement.
  - Added explicit signed-HMAC lifecycle enforcement for verifier-supplied HMAC
    selectors, allowing rotated keys to verify old material while revoked and
    expired selectors reject before MAC verification.
  - Expanded signed-HMAC witness golden vectors to freeze lifecycle status,
    accepted and rejected event sets, and lifecycle rejection diagnostics for
    trusted, rotated, revoked, and expired HMAC selectors.
  - Added a signed-HMAC public-trust bridge poison fixture proving public
    `GOFTP-TRUST/1` rows cannot authorize `k1.` HMAC selectors or revoke
    explicit HMAC selectors, while unsigned replay remains unchanged.
  - Promoted the signed-HMAC public-trust bridge into public golden vectors,
    binding advisory `GOFTP-KEY/1` and `GOFTP-TRUST/1` fixture text to both the
    rejected `k1.` selector case and the accepted explicit HMAC selector case
    without leaking the fixture HMAC secret.
  - Routed the executable source-art smoke surface through `GobanFTP::Witness`,
    so it displays `event_set_root`, replay status, board hash, SGF hash, and
    diagnostics without owning protocol truth.
  - Added a witness/projection-only surface renderer that formats fields already
    produced by `GobanFTP::Witness` and projection text without reading storage,
    parsing events, recomputing roots, or deciding profile acceptance.
  - Added `gobanftp v1 witness --surface text|html` as a read-only CLI
    inspection surface over the existing witness result and its already-rendered
    projection text.
  - Added a golden smoke for the minimal `v1 witness --surface` text and static
    HTML outputs, freezing their digests and canonical projection sections.
  - Added `gobanftp v1 witness --surface terminal` as a static terminal
    observatory over the same witness result, freezing its minimal digest while
    avoiding any interactive TUI claim.
  - Extended the public showcase smoke gate to cover the text, static HTML, and
    static terminal witness surfaces alongside the shrine, race, source-art, and
    default v1 witness paths.
  - Added a P14 release-gate dry-run report documenting the command matrix,
    pass/skip status, generated artifacts, and remaining non-release claims
    without tagging v1.0 or declaring P14 complete.
  - Tightened manifest skip rules so detached-worktree `.git` files and local
    scratch suffixes are excluded without dropping intentional attack fixtures
    under `t/fixtures/`.
  - Added a P14 release manifest and tag plan, then clarified it as the
    then-active v1.0/P14 development release plan after the local `v0.2` /
    package `0.002` candidate was skipped in favor of continuing directly
    toward v1.0/P14, while separating the `1.000_001` development freeze
    matrix from the final reserved `v1.0` / package `1.000` release identity.
  - Prepared and then skipped the local v0.2 / package 0.002 release candidate,
    keeping v1.0/P14 as the active release route.
  - Clarified the next golden-vector and P14 claim-audit slice after Git-tree
    and DNS-record runtime read admission, without claiming Git publish, live
    DNS, DNS publish, hosted Web UI, interactive TUI, or v1.0/P14 completion.
  - Added a synthetic DAG-boundary golden vector for `event_id_collision`,
    without claiming an ordinary GOFTP/1 basename hash collision.
  - Added the first public non-consensus-poison golden vector, binding the
    WebDAV metadata-poison fixture to unchanged event-set preimage, root,
    replay, board, projection text, and SGF truth.
  - Added core/local public non-consensus-poison golden vectors for bad mtime,
    bad payload bytes, bad listing order, poisoned sidecar, stale projections,
    and temporary publish debris, binding self-contained evidence artifacts
    where the poison is not part of listing names.
  - Added a WebDAV href-traversal public non-consensus-poison golden vector,
    binding raw and percent-encoded traversal href fixture input names to
    unchanged one-event event-set preimage, root, replay, board, projection
    text, and SGF truth.
  - Added a DNS owner-poison public non-consensus-poison golden vector, binding
    real record fixture input names to unchanged event-set preimage, root,
    replay, board, projection text, and SGF truth.
  - Added a Git-tree public non-consensus-poison golden vector and generalized
    the poison-vector harness so each row declares its own ignored evidence and
    optional poisoned listing order, without claiming Git publish, remote fetch,
    or provider APIs.
  - Added an FTP listing-shadow public non-consensus-poison golden vector,
    binding FTP-shaped sidecar, tmp, projection, recursive descendant, and
    list-order rows to unchanged event-set preimage, root, replay, board,
    projection text, and SGF truth without claiming live FTP, `RETR`, `SIZE`,
    `MDTM`, FTP auth, FTP integrity, or publish behavior.
  - Refreshed the P14 claim-audit and clean-gate plan after the FTP public
    poison vector, adding profile attack/publish gates and tarball checks for
    shipped public poison-vector evidence without tagging or declaring v1.0
    complete.
  - Normalized `MANIFEST` ordering so a clean-checkout `make manifest` gate
    leaves no tracked diff.
  - Recorded a successful clean-checkout `1.000_001` development freeze matrix
    as development evidence only, leaving v1.0 untagged and reserving the final
    `v1.0` / package `1.000` artifact path for a separate stable matrix.

0.001  2026-05-17
  - Treat this distribution as the v0.1 hardening/showcase release: the Perl
    package version is `0.001`, while the project milestone name is `v0.1`.
  - Built the initial GOFTP/1 runtime prototype: descriptor and event filename
    parsing, event id calculation, DAG replay, rules validation, SGF output,
    rebuildable projections, local CLI play/publish/watch commands, local
    storage, and a mock-tested FTP store backend.
  - Kept core replay listing-first: descriptor and events/ basenames remain
    authoritative, while file bytes, FTP metadata, sidecars, projections, and
    temporary entries stay outside consensus input.
  - Added ack-assisted fork recovery commands while preserving conservative
    fork diagnostics by default.
  - Added release hygiene rules for Inline::C caches, blib, MYMETA,
    pm_to_blib, generated distributions, and temporary publish/build scratch
    files.
  - Added a minimal replayable example fixture with rebuildable projections.
  - Removed unused JSON::MaybeXS and Path::Tiny runtime dependency
    declarations and synchronized the dependency documentation.
  - Documented make disttest and the requirement to run live FTP tests against
    an isolated, disposable FTP root.
  - Added an opt-in `script/live-ftp-smoke` helper that runs the live FTP tests
    against a temporary localhost pyftpdlib server without making pyftpdlib a
    default test dependency.
  - Documented the v0.1 hardening/showcase boundary: `GOFTP/1` consensus stays
    frozen for the release, and the listing transcript is a replay-derived
    projection rather than a consensus input.
  - Added a browsable `ftp-race-shrine` example fixture that shows a conservative
    fork after an FTP-style race while keeping ack-assisted recovery explicit.
